      <div type="clause" n="III 4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:InCn">In Cn</ref> III 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="In Cn III 4" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="613" ed="#liebermann"/>Et si quis calumniatur, quasi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.17"/> ducat exercitum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.18"/> super aliquem, et negauerit, purget se secundum prętium calumniantis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.e"/> aut eum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.5"/> persoluat.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 613 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">613</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mundbrece III 56; calumnians <hi rend="italic">ist hier und</hi> III 4 der Geschädigte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mundbrece III 56; calumnians here and in III 4 is the injured party</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">613</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt LbSCt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in LbSCt</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">613</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quia <hi rend="italic">LbSCt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quia LbSCt</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="InCn_III-4.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">613</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suum <hi rend="italic">fügt zu S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">suum added by S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="InCn_III-4.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Verf. missversteht Ine's <hi rend="italic">hine</hi> (‘sich’) als ‘ihn, den Erschlagenen’, und bezieht <hi rend="italic">his</hi> irrig auf den Kläger statt Beklagten. Die Eidesschwere (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8. 9) der Reinigung hängt von des Klägers Klageeid ab, und dieser kann vom Wergelde abhängen. Auch dies ungenau</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The author misunderstands Ine’s <hi rend="italic">hine</hi> (‘himself’) as ‘him, the slain man’, and wrongly refers <hi rend="italic">his</hi> to the plaintiff instead of the defendant. The weight of the oath (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8. 9) of exculpation depends on the plaintiff’s oath of accusation, and this may depend on the wergild. This too is inexact</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
